  <worksheet>
    <title> Session #6 (Sections 3.6, 3.7, &amp; 3.8, Appendix K.1 &amp; K.2)</title>
    <p>
      Directions: Answer each of the following as best you can. Feel free to discuss your thoughts about the questions with some peers around you.
    </p>
    <paragraphs> <!--   %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%   SECTION 2  %%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%    -->
      <title>Getting Warmed Up and in the Right Mindset</title>
      <exercise><!-- #1 -->
        <statement>
          <p>
            Match each of the following expressions to its corresponding graph. Think about identifying characteristics for each graph, i.e. asymptotes, interecepts, etc.
          </p>
          <sidebyside widths="33.333% 33.333% 33.333%" valign="middle">
            <p>
              <ol marker="(A)">
                <li>
                  <p>
                    <image source="output/h6fig1" width="100%">
                      <shortdescription>Graph of a function plotted on coordinate axes. Refer to image description for more detail.</shortdescription><!--This is what a screenreader reads. Do not include math mode here.-->
                      <description><!--this is not automatically read by a screenreader, but user can navigate there. Math mode is acceptable here and paragraph environment must be included-->
                        <p>
                        A graph of a function plotted on coordinate axes with <m>x</m>-values ranging from <m>-4</m> to <m>4</m> and <m>y</m>-values ranging from <m>-4</m> to <m>4</m>. 
                        The function has a horizontal asymptote at <m>y=-2</m>, crosses the <m>x</m>-axis between <m>x=-2</m> and <m>x=-1</m>, and crosses the <m>y</m>-axis at <m>y=-1</m>. 
                        </p>
